# Example ReRDMFT input file: Ne, cc-pVDZ, X2C, FUNCTIONAL PCCD, FULL_OPTIMIZATION.
# CHOLESKY TRUE: X2C's 2*n_spatial = 30-dimensional spinor problem is cheap either way, but this
# matches the C4_DHF companion example (ne_pccd_c4.inp), where it matters more.
#
# CAVEAT: X2C_HF.h's own SCF is a DELIBERATELY approximate X2C (one-electron-only picture change,
# no two-electron picture-change correction at all -- see its own header comment). For a basis
# with d (or higher) angular momentum functions, like cc-pVDZ here, this approximation's error is
# much larger than for an s/p-only basis (see examples/lih_pccd_x2c.inp, where it is < 1 mHa): the
# "Max |E_X2C_approx - E_DHF|" check this run prints is ~0.064 Ha for Ne, even though EXACT X2C
# matches 4-component DHF to 1e-10 Ha. The pCCD *correlation energy* on top of this approximate
# reference is still accurate (it agrees with the NON_REL and C4_DHF correlation energy to better
# than 1e-5 Ha -- see ne_pccd_c4.inp's own header), but the TOTAL energy below should NOT be read
# as a relativistic reference value for Ne; use ne_pccd_c4.inp (exact 4-component) for that.
NELEC 10
BASIS ne-cc-pvdz.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PCCD
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
Ne  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
END
